            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-pathdup",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/reviewresult/rules.go:94-110",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "checkPaths compares inspected and diff paths as sets, so a reviewer reply that lists the same path twice, or a binding with duplicate paths, is accepted. The contract says one entry per path, but duplicates in the reply are not tested or refused. This is low impact because coverage of the diff is still proven.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/reviewresult/rules.go:94-110"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "R3-nulluniq",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/reviewresult/wire.go:104-125",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "checkShape does not check that array elements are non-null. A null inside paths, proof_refs or evidence decodes silently to an empty string. A severe finding with proof_refs of [null] would be refused only because the string is blank. A null in paths is refused only as a path mismatch. The behavior is safe but untested.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/reviewresult/wire.go:104-125"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Read all 17 changed paths in full.",
              "Parse applies its rules in a fixed order. Each refusal returns the zero Result and wraps exactly one named error. The tests cover each rule and the rule ordering.",
              "The shape check rejects duplicate keys, case-variant member names, nulls and missing members. These cases are covered in parse_test.go.",
              "The new skills test requires Parse to accept the object the reviewer delta spells out, which guards against drift between prompt and parser.",
              "No blocker or critical regression found: the changes are additive. The only existing behavior that changes is the reviewer prompt, which now includes id, and the pinned tests were updated to match."
            ]
          }
